---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy & Cookie Notice · Puffs of Smoke"
  description="How analytics, cookies, and personal data are handled on Puffs of Smoke."
>
  <header class="page-header container-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy & cookie notice</h1>
    <p class="page-header__lede">A plain-language explanation of the limited information this site collects.</p>
    <p class="page-updated">Last updated November 14, 2025</p>
  </header>

  <article class="prose prose--page privacy-page container-article">
    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <p>
      I use Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate traffic patterns such as page views, referral sources, and
      approximate location. Analytics remains disabled unless you choose “Allow analytics” in the consent notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside of analytics, the site stores only preferences you choose—such as appearance and analytics consent—in
      your browser. I do not sell personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics cookies load only after you opt in. The site also uses local storage for the appearance setting
      (<code>theme</code>) and your analytics choice (<code>analytics-consent</code>). These remain on your device until
      you clear the site’s browser data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use “Manage cookies” in the footer to reopen the consent notice.</li>
      <li>Use your browser’s privacy controls to disable or remove cookies.</li>
      <li>Decline analytics and continue using every part of the site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is unclear, email <a href="mailto:hello@jonkohlmeier.com">hello@jonkohlmeier.com</a> or use the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
